<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="tour-detail-layout">
  <!-- Main content -->
  <div class="tour-detail-main reveal">
    <h2>Tour Overview</h2>
    <p>Follow the legendary Hexi Corridor on this 8-day private journey from Lanzhou to Urumqi. This historic passage, once the lifeline of the Silk Road, connects a string of oases between the Gobi Desert and the Qilian Mountains. From the rainbow-colored Zhangye Danxia to the Buddhist treasure house of Mogao Caves, and from the westernmost Great Wall fortress to the desert oasis of Turpan, this itinerary captures the very essence of the ancient Silk Road.</p>

    <div class="highlight-box"><h3>Trip Highlights</h3><ul>
      <li>Marvel at the rainbow mountains of Zhangye Danxia</li><li>Stand at Jiayuguan — the Great Wall's western terminus</li>
      <li>Explore the Mogao Caves in Dunhuang</li><li>Camel ride on the Singing Sand Dunes</li>
      <li>Visit the ancient Jiaohe Ruins in Turpan</li><li>Discover the Flaming Mountains and Grape Valley</li>
      <li>Experience the Karez underground irrigation system</li>
      <li>End your journey in vibrant Urumqi</li>
    </ul></div>

    <h2>Day-by-Day Itinerary</h2>
    <ul class="itinerary">
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>1</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Arrive in Lanzhou</h4><p>Arrive in Lanzhou, the capital of Gansu Province and gateway to the Hexi Corridor. Transfer to your hotel. Evening walk along the Yellow River waterfront and visit the iconic Iron Bridge.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Lanzhou 4★</span><span>🍽 Dinner</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>2</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Lanzhou → Zhangye (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning high-speed train to Zhangye (approx. 3 hours). Afternoon visit to the Zhangye Danxia Landform — the famous rainbow-colored rock formations, best photographed in late afternoon light. These stunning geological layers create a natural canvas of red, orange, and yellow hues.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Zhangye 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>3</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Zhangye → Jiayuguan</h4><p>Morning visit to the Giant Buddha Temple, home to China's largest reclining Buddha. Drive to Jiayuguan (2.5 hours). Afternoon at the Jiayuguan Fortress — the mighty western gate of the Ming Dynasty Great Wall, standing alone against the vast Gobi Desert.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Jiayuguan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>4</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Jiayuguan → Dunhuang</h4><p>Morning visit to the Overhanging Great Wall and the First Beacon Tower. Drive through the Gobi Desert to Dunhuang (5 hours), the legendary Silk Road oasis that guarded the gateway to Central Asia.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>5</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang — Mogao Caves & Singing Sand Dunes</h4><p>A full day at two UNESCO sites. Morning at the Mogao Caves — a millennium of Buddhist art preserved in nearly 500 grottoes. Afternoon camel ride through the Singing Sand Dunes, followed by sunset at the Crescent Moon Spring, a miraculous oasis in the desert.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Dunhuang 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>6</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Dunhuang → Turpan (High-speed train)</h4><p>Morning high-speed train to Turpan (approx. 4 hours). Afternoon visit to the ancient Jiaohe Ruins — a city carved from raw earth that thrived for over 1,600 years. Learn about the ingenious Karez irrigation system that made desert farming possible.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Turpan 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>7</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Turpan → Urumqi</h4><p>Morning at the Flaming Mountains and the lush Grape Valley, where vines grow in the desert shade. Visit the Emin Minaret, the tallest minaret in China. Afternoon drive to Urumqi (3 hours). Evening at the bustling Erdaoqiao Grand Bazaar.</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🏨 Urumqi 4★</span><span>🍽 B/L/D</span></div></div></li>
      <li><div class="day-badge"><strong>8</strong>Day</div><div class="day-content"><h4>Depart Urumqi</h4><p>Morning visit to the Xinjiang Regional Museum, home to the famous Tarim mummies. Free time until your airport transfer. Your Hexi Corridor journey concludes. 再见!</p><div class="day-meta"><span>🍽 B</span></div></div></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What's Included</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>7 nights 4-star hotel accommodation (twin-share)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>English-speaking private guide throughout</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All high-speed trains per itinerary</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Private air-conditioned vehicle & driver</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Meals as indicated (B=Breakfast, L=Lunch, D=Dinner)</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>All entrance fees & listed activities</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Airport transfers on arrival & departure</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item good"><span class="icon">✓</span><p>Travel insurance (China domestic)</p></div>
    </div>

    <h2>What's Excluded</h2>
    <div class="inc-list">
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>International flights to/from China</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Chinese visa fees</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Personal expenses & tips</p></div>
      <div class="inc-item bad"><span class="icon">✗</span><p>Single room supplement ($280)</p></div>
    </div>

    </div>

